From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:26:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xgameruntime: Treat HANDLER_NOT_SET as no completion handler
 in XAsync.

completed is HANDLER_NOT_SET, (void *)~0, until put_Completed() sets a handler, but three places
used it as one: put_Completed() assigned completed to its argument instead of the reverse and
AddRef()ed the sentinel, the completion callback invoked it, and the last Release() released it.
Each crashed at 0xffffffffffffffff, as every operation started without a handler did on
completion. Assign the handler in put_Completed() and skip the sentinel elsewhere, keeping it on
completion so that a handler set later is still invoked.

Original work for macrock (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: async-handler
---
 include/private/IXAsync.hpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/private/IXAsync.hpp b/include/private/IXAsync.hpp
index 5ccecfa421ec75aa6a8728f7f82f9b258d3b1482..7fe17e543e5b5eeb4d281f078b4801dddc248a3e 100644
--- a/include/private/IXAsync.hpp
+++ b/include/private/IXAsync.hpp
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ public:
 
         if ( !curr )
         {
-            if ( completed )
+            if ( completed && completed != HANDLER_NOT_SET )
             {
                 completed->Release();
             }
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ public:
                 return E_ILLEGAL_DELEGATE_ASSIGNMENT;
 
             // Keep the routine alive until invokation.
-            routine = completed;
+            completed = routine;
             routine->AddRef();
 
             if ( status > Started )
@@ -306,7 +306,11 @@ private:
         {
             const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock( impl->lock );
             handler = impl->completed;
-            impl->completed = nullptr;
+            /* Without a handler yet, put_Completed() invokes the one set later. */
+            if ( handler == HANDLER_NOT_SET )
+                handler = nullptr;
+            else
+                impl->completed = nullptr;
         }
         if ( handler )
         {
